    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0526" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 422.11G93/956</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hartman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-19T14:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your June 12, 4 p.m. You may hand the following memorandum to Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs in unofficial manner saying that it has been presented to
                    Ecuadoran Minister in Washington.</p>
                <p>[Here follows the above memorandum of June 19, 1918, to the Ecuadoran
                    Minister.]</p>
                <p>Keep the Department advised daily in regard to any developments in situation. The
                    Department has kept Norton, now at Panama, informed of this matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
